```

This is indeed incorrect. Can you post the whole ptx for completeness? This is not what I expect as the output from the WGMMA pipelining pass.

The PTX I was working with is here https://gist.github.com/masahi/d1d7f2f14a616ddaff9e6d8a5c199c66. The structure of the kernel looks like
```
W_bf16 = upcast W_mxfp4, scales 
w1, w2, ... w8 = split W_bf16 // split into 8 pieces along K dim

mov w1', w1
wgmma w1', x1, acc  // w1 is reg, x1 is smem
commit_group
wait 7

mov w2', w2
wgmma w2', x2, acc
commit_group
wait 7
.
.
.
mov w8', w8
wgmma w8', x8, acc
commit_group
wait 7
```
Each wait 7 is supposed to ensure that, at each iteration, a wgmma op from the previous iteration is finished before the LHS operand is overwritten for the corresponding wgmma op in the current iteration.

We see that
* At the start of the loop, the second wgmma op from the prev iteration is still in flight
* WGMMA in the second commit group uses registers LHS `%r1303,%r1304,%r1305,%r1306` https://gist.github.com/masahi/d1d7f2f14a616ddaff9e6d8a5c199c66#file-moe_h20_racy-ptx-L1473
* Which are overwritten at https://gist.github.com/masahi/d1d7f2f14a616ddaff9e6d8a5c199c66#file-moe_h20_racy-ptx-L1460-L1463
* This overwrite is safe thanks to `wait_group 7` at https://gist.github.com/masahi/d1d7f2f14a616ddaff9e6d8a5c199c66#file-moe_h20_racy-ptx-L1457

